1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:19,600
Welcome to Update 17 of AHEAD Pathway: the Rehearsal room. It is a practice panel that has read your own work, and it is now open to every candidate. Use it before a presentation, and use it in between, as a place to think aloud about your research.

2
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:53,870
Open the Rehearsal room and choose what you are preparing for: a proposal defence, the Research Degrees Weekend, an ethics committee, an oral examination, or a conference talk. Choose ten, twenty or thirty minutes, and a supportive, typical or demanding panel. The Director reads each rehearsal, so that together we can see what helps and keep improving the room. It is still practice: no marks, and nothing enters your record unless you save it.

3
00:00:55,270 --> 00:01:21,479
Three panel members ask one question at a time: a Chair for the big picture, a methodologist for design and ethics, and a specialist reader for literature and framework. Every question is grounded in your own proposal and in the feedback you have had, and tells you what it draws on. Answer aloud, or type. Your spoken words become text, and the recording is not kept.

4
00:01:22,879 --> 00:01:40,549
At the end comes a debrief: for every answer, what was genuinely strong, what was missing, and the points a stronger answer would cover. Never a script to memorise. Practise any single question again, and the panel follows up until it is clear.

5
00:01:41,949 --> 00:02:11,159
Use the room often, not only before a presentation. After you upload a new chapter, let the panel test it. Practise explaining your framework or your method aloud until it comes naturally. Prepare for a supervision meeting. Find the weak spot in an argument before an examiner does. Each round remembers the last one, so the panel returns to what was weak, and you can see yourself improve.

6
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:25,530
Fifteen minutes in the Rehearsal room, once a week, will change how you speak about your research. That is AHEAD Pathway: your degree, well supported, every step of the way.
